+"""Qwen3.5 exportable modules for speculative decoding (MTP).
+
+Activated by `extra_kwargs={"mtp_speculative": {"num_draft_steps": G,
+"ring_size": R}}` (R must be >= G+2). Adds, on top of the external-embedder
+prefill/decode modules:
+
+  - a `verify` signature: a prefill-shaped graph over G+1 positions with
+    embeddings input, per-position fp32 `logits` and post-final-norm fp32
+    `activations` outputs — the LiteRT-LM MTP drafter contract
+    (llm_litert_mtp_drafter.cc: verify's rank-1 input_pos length IS G+1);
+  - `activations` output on decode (the runtime seeds the first draft of each
+    decode turn from it);
+  - three extra state buffers threaded through every signature:
+      kv_cache_k_mtp / kv_cache_v_mtp — the drafter's teacher-forced KV cache.
+        Slot q holds k/v of x_q = mtp.fc(cat(mtp_norm_e(emb(t_{q+1})),
+        mtp_norm_h(h_q))) at RoPE position q — exactly the `fixed`-mode
+        drafter contract measured in P0 (drafter queries at rope p-1 attend
+        slots <= p-2 plus themselves). Every graph writes, for each of its
+        input positions q, slot q-1 from (embedding row q, h_{q-1}); h_{q-1}
+        of the first position comes from the hidden ring. Rejected-draft
+        slots are garbage until the next round's verify overwrites them,
+        and are never attended before that (the drafter's attend limit
+        p-2 never passes the last verified position).
+      kv_cache_h_mtp — hidden ring [R, 1, hidden]: post-final-norm h_q at
+        slot q mod R. Prefill writes its last VALID h; decode writes h_s;
+        verify writes all G+1 (the accept point is unknown at graph time).
+
+The gated-delta conv/recurrent ring itself lives in the shared cache layer
+(cache.py); these modules only add the drafter-side state and outputs.
+"""
